208:  *  values replaces the node's original transformation matrix at a
209:  *  specific time.
210:  *  This means all keys are absolute and not relative to the bone default pose.
211:  *  The order in which the transformations are applied is
212:  *  - as usual - scaling, rotation, translation.
213:  *
214:  *  @note All keys are returned in their correct, chronological order.
215:  *  Duplicate keys don't pass the validation step. Most likely there
216:  *  will be no negative time values, but they are not forbidden also ( so
217:  *  implementations need to cope with them! ) */
