  993:  Q: Where is the documentation?
  994:  A: This library is poorly documented at the moment and expects the user to be acquainted with C/C++.
  995:     - Run the examples/ applications and explore them.
  996:     - Read Getting Started (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki/Getting-Started) guide.
  997:     - See demo code in imgui_demo.cpp and particularly the ImGui::ShowDemoWindow() function.
  998:     - The demo covers most features of Dear ImGui, so you can read the code and see its output.
  999:     - See documentation and comments at the top of imgui.cpp + effectively imgui.h.
 1000:     - 20+ standalone example applications using e.g. OpenGL/DirectX are provided in the
 1001:       examples/ folder to explain how to integrate Dear ImGui with your own engine/application.
 1002:     - The Wiki (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki) has many resources and links.
 1003:     - The Glossary (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki/Glossary) page also may be useful.
 1004:     - Your programming IDE is your friend, find the type or function declaration to find comments
 1005:       associated with it.
