 9574: // Called by IMGUI_CHECKVERSION().
 9575: // Verify that the type sizes are matching between the calling file's compilation unit and imgui.cpp's compilation unit
 9576: // If this triggers you have mismatched headers and compiled code versions.
 9577: // - It could be because of a build issue (using new headers with old compiled code)
 9578: // - It could be because of mismatched configuration #define, compilation settings, packing pragma etc.
 9579: //   THE CONFIGURATION SETTINGS MENTIONED IN imconfig.h MUST BE SET FOR ALL COMPILATION UNITS INVOLVED WITH DEAR IMGUI.
 9580: //   Which is why it is required you put them in your imconfig file (and NOT only before including imgui.h).
 9581: //   Otherwise it is possible that different compilation units would see different structure layout.
