 9595: // Until 1.89 (August 2022, IMGUI_VERSION_NUM < 18814) it was legal to use SetCursorPos()/SetCursorScreenPos()
 9596: // to extend contents size of our parent container (e.g. window contents size, which is used for auto-resizing
 9597: // windows, table column contents size used for auto-resizing columns, group size).
 9598: // This was causing issues and ambiguities and we needed to retire that.
 9599: // From 1.89, extending contents size boundaries REQUIRES AN ITEM TO BE SUBMITTED.
 9600: //
 9601: //  Previously this would make the window content size ~200x200:
 9602: //    Begin(...) + SetCursorScreenPos(GetCursorScreenPos() + ImVec2(200,200)) + End();                      // NOT OK ANYMORE
 9603: //  Instead, please submit an item:
 9604: //    Begin(...) + SetCursorScreenPos(GetCursorScreenPos() + ImVec2(200,200)) + Dummy(ImVec2(0,0)) + End(); // OK
 9605: //  Alternative:
 9606: //    Begin(...) + Dummy(ImVec2(200,200)) + End(); // OK
 9607: //
 9608: // The assert below detects when the _last_ call in a window was a SetCursorPos() not followed by an Item,
 9609: // and with a position that would grow the parent contents size.
 9610: //
 9611: // Advanced:
 9612: // - For reference, old logic was causing issues because it meant that SetCursorScreenPos(GetCursorScreenPos())
 9613: //   had a side-effect on layout! In particular this caused problem to compute group boundaries.
 9614: //   e.g. BeginGroup() + SomeItem() + SetCursorScreenPos(GetCursorScreenPos()) + EndGroup() would cause the
 9615: //   group to be taller because auto-sizing generally adds padding on bottom and right side.
 9616: // - While this code is a little twisted, no-one would expect SetXXX(GetXXX()) to have a side-effect.
 9617: //   Using vertical alignment patterns would frequently trigger this sorts of issue.
 9618: // - See https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/issues/5548 for more details.
