 803:     // Tables
 804:     // - Full-featured replacement for old Columns API.
 805:     // - See Demo->Tables for demo code. See top of imgui_tables.cpp for general commentary.
 806:     // - See ImGuiTableFlags_ and ImGuiTableColumnFlags_ enums for a description of available flags.
 807:     // The typical call flow is:
 808:     // - 1. Call BeginTable(), early out if returning false.
 809:     // - 2. Optionally call TableSetupColumn() to submit column name/flags/defaults.
 810:     // - 3. Optionally call TableSetupScrollFreeze() to request scroll freezing of columns/rows.
 811:     // - 4. Optionally call TableHeadersRow() to submit a header row. Names are pulled from TableSetupColumn() data.
 812:     // - 5. Populate contents:
 813:     //    - In most situations you can use TableNextRow() + TableSetColumnIndex(N) to start appending into a column.
 814:     //    - If you are using tables as a sort of grid, where every column is holding the same type of contents,
 815:     //      you may prefer using TableNextColumn() instead of TableNextRow() + TableSetColumnIndex().
 816:     //      TableNextColumn() will automatically wrap-around into the next row if needed.
 817:     //    - IMPORTANT: Comparatively to the old Columns() API, we need to call TableNextColumn() for the first column!
 818:     //    - Summary of possible call flow:
 819:     //        - TableNextRow() -> TableSetColumnIndex(0) -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableSetColumnIndex(1) -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK
 820:     //        - TableNextRow() -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK
 821:     //        -                   TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK: TableNextColumn() automatically gets to next row!
 822:     //        - TableNextRow()                           -> Text("Hello 0")                                               // Not OK! Missing TableSetColumnIndex() or TableNextColumn()! Text will not appear!
 823:     // - 5. Call EndTable()
 824:     IMGUI_API bool          BeginTable(const char* str_id, int columns, ImGuiTableFlags flags = 0, const ImVec2& outer_size = ImVec2(0.0f, 0.0f), float inner_width = 0.0f);
