 969:     // Inputs Utilities: Shortcut Testing & Routing [BETA]
 970:     // - ImGuiKeyChord = a ImGuiKey + optional ImGuiMod_Alt/ImGuiMod_Ctrl/ImGuiMod_Shift/ImGuiMod_Super.
 971:     //       ImGuiKey_C                          // Accepted by functions taking ImGuiKey or ImGuiKeyChord arguments
 972:     //       ImGuiMod_Ctrl | ImGuiKey_C          // Accepted by functions taking ImGuiKeyChord arguments
 973:     //   only ImGuiMod_XXX values are legal to combine with an ImGuiKey. You CANNOT combine two ImGuiKey values.
 974:     // - The general idea is that several callers may register interest in a shortcut, and only one owner gets it.
 975:     //      Parent   -> call Shortcut(Ctrl+S)    // When Parent is focused, Parent gets the shortcut.
 976:     //        Child1 -> call Shortcut(Ctrl+S)    // When Child1 is focused, Child1 gets the shortcut (Child1 overrides Parent shortcuts)
 977:     //        Child2 -> no call                  // When Child2 is focused, Parent gets the shortcut.
 978:     //   The whole system is order independent, so if Child1 makes its calls before Parent, results will be identical.
 979:     //   This is an important property as it facilitate working with foreign code or larger codebase.
 980:     // - To understand the difference:
 981:     //   - IsKeyChordPressed() compares mods and call IsKeyPressed() -> function has no side-effect.
 982:     //   - Shortcut() submits a route, routes are resolved, if it currently can be routed it calls IsKeyChordPressed() -> function has (desirable) side-effects as it can prevents another call from getting the route.
