1827: //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1828: // [SECTION] Tables API flags and structures (ImGuiTableFlags, ImGuiTableColumnFlags, ImGuiTableRowFlags, ImGuiTableBgTarget, ImGuiTableSortSpecs, ImGuiTableColumnSortSpecs)
1829: //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1830: // Flags for ImGui::BeginTable()
1831: // - Important! Sizing policies have complex and subtle side effects, much more so than you would expect.
1832: //   Read comments/demos carefully + experiment with live demos to get acquainted with them.
1833: // - The DEFAULT sizing policies are:
1834: //    - Default to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedFit    if ScrollX is on, or if host window has ImGuiWindowFlags_AlwaysAutoResize.
1835: //    - Default to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame if ScrollX is off.
1836: // - When ScrollX is off:
1837: //    - Table defaults to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame -> all Columns defaults to ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch with same weight.
1838: //    - Columns sizing policy allowed: Stretch (default), Fixed/Auto.
1839: //    - Fixed Columns (if any) will generally obtain their requested width (unless the table cannot fit them all).
1840: //    - Stretch Columns will share the remaining width according to their respective weight.
1841: //    - Mixed Fixed/Stretch columns is possible but has various side-effects on resizing behaviors.
1842: //      The typical use of mixing sizing policies is: any number of LEADING Fixed columns, followed by one or two TRAILING Stretch columns.
1843: //      (this is because the visible order of columns have subtle but necessary effects on how they react to manual resizing).
1844: // - When ScrollX is on:
1845: //    - Table defaults to ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedFit -> all Columns defaults to ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed
1846: //    - Columns sizing policy allowed: Fixed/Auto mostly.
1847: //    - Fixed Columns can be enlarged as needed. Table will show a horizontal scrollbar if needed.
1848: //    - When using auto-resizing (non-resizable) fixed columns, querying the content width to use item right-alignment e.g. SetNextItemWidth(-FLT_MIN) doesn't make sense, would create a feedback loop.
1849: //    - Using Stretch columns OFTEN DOES NOT MAKE SENSE if ScrollX is on, UNLESS you have specified a value for 'inner_width' in BeginTable().
1850: //      If you specify a value for 'inner_width' then effectively the scrolling space is known and Stretch or mixed Fixed/Stretch columns become meaningful again.
1851: // - Read on documentation at the top of imgui_tables.cpp for details.
1852: enum ImGuiTableFlags_
1853: {
1854:     // Features
1855:     ImGuiTableFlags_None                       = 0,
1856:     ImGuiTableFlags_Resizable                  = 1 << 0,   // Enable resizing columns.
1857:     ImGuiTableFlags_Reorderable                = 1 << 1,   // Enable reordering columns in header row (need calling TableSetupColumn() + TableHeadersRow() to display headers)
1858:     ImGuiTableFlags_Hideable                   = 1 << 2,   // Enable hiding/disabling columns in context menu.
1859:     ImGuiTableFlags_Sortable                   = 1 << 3,   // Enable sorting. Call TableGetSortSpecs() to obtain sort specs. Also see ImGuiTableFlags_SortMulti and ImGuiTableFlags_SortTristate.
1860:     ImGuiTableFlags_NoSavedSettings            = 1 << 4,   // Disable persisting columns order, width, visibility and sort settings in the .ini file.
1861:     ImGuiTableFlags_ContextMenuInBody          = 1 << 5,   // Right-click on columns body/contents will display table context menu. By default it is available in TableHeadersRow().
1862:     // Decorations
1863:     ImGuiTableFlags_RowBg                      = 1 << 6,   // Set each RowBg color with ImGuiCol_TableRowBg or ImGuiCol_TableRowBgAlt (equivalent of calling TableSetBgColor with ImGuiTableBgFlags_RowBg0 on each row manually)
1864:     ImGuiTableFlags_BordersInnerH              = 1 << 7,   // Draw horizontal borders between rows.
1865:     ImGuiTableFlags_BordersOuterH              = 1 << 8,   // Draw horizontal borders at the top and bottom.
